{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Unto me you shall come, for I have surely hired you.</b> And you will do no wrong in this to nullify my sister's conjugal right, since this is done with her knowledge and consent. And through this narrative, which appears disgraceful in the eyes of those who find fault in the Torah, He has in truth made known to us that the matter of procreation among the Patriarchs was as it was with Adam and his wife before their sin — for their intent in it was not at all for their own gratification, but rather to raise up seed solely for the honor of their Creator and for His service. And He made known that since the intent of the Matriarchs was desirable before El blessed be He in their efforts to acquire the mandrakes and the matter of the mandrakes, their prayer concerning this was heard — for it is fitting for the righteous person to make every possible natural effort to attain his purpose, and along with this to pray that he attain the end, as they said of blessed memory (Yevamot 64a) that the Holy One blessed be He desires the prayer of the righteous." "<b>And he lay with her that night.</b> Of his own will, when he saw Leah's diligence and the goodness of her intent in this."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:32.495515159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}